00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:27.990
I can't believe Maeshima
would rush out like that.

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:29.990
Right? It was unexpected.

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:33.660
But did the captain and Yuki have to go, too?

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.200
Well, you know?

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:39.490
With just Maeshima and Sasugai,
who knows what they'd end up doing?

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:40.700
That's true.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:42.450
Just because Terauchi and the others aren't here

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:43.490
doesn't mean you can slack off.

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:45.080
--Yes, sir!
--Okay.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:49.740
Coach, the captain said they'd go to the school
Himekawa transferred to for now.

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:50.910
Very well.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.040
Kubota, you go join practice, too.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.330
Yes, sir!

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:58.120
Come to think of it,
where'd Himekawa go, anyway?

00:03:58.120 --> 00:03:59.910
Um, I think...

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:00.740
Niigata?

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:01.300
Rice?

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:02.080
Ski resorts.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:02.990
Cold-season yellowtail.

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:04.330
Uesugi Kenshin.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.850
Niigata Station

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:08.120
Speaking of which, Sasu, why were you in Osaka?

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.080
There's a choreographer I know there.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:12.290
I went to ask for advice
about a lead-focused routine.

