00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:04.940
"Coach Introduction"
"Keiji Kumada"

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:00.450
Keiji Kumada.

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:03.080
A coach highly praised for training juniors,

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:05.490
but in the end, that's all he's known for.

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:08.330
Why did Himekawa choose this school?

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:12.200
It makes me happy that you're so
interested in me that you'd look me up.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:17.790
Most of the students here are former
members of the junior club I taught at.

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:19.450
When the high school asked me to coach here,

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:23.040
I got in touch with them
and asked them to join me.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.830
Izumi was a member of the same club.

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:29.370
I asked if he wanted to come here when
he was taking his high school entrance exams,

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:31.370
but he refused.

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:33.450
I'm not planning to make
a living figure skating,

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:36.370
so I don't plan on being that serious about it.

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:38.370
I don't know what happened
when he was with you all,

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:40.830
but in the end, he came to me.

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:42.660
He even got permission
to change clubs from the Federation,

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:46.990
so I think we'll be able to thank you
at nationals one of these days.

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:49.240
What a crafty old man.

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:52.410
Thank you very much!

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:57.080
You're still here?

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:59.950
You made us wait this long,
and then you give us that attitude?!

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:02.120
Sorry, but I still need to practice.

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:04.160
You're practicing late by yourself?

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:08.240
You're really different from the Himekawa
who used to leave exactly on time.

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:10.410
What's with this change of heart?

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:12.990
Go talk to them.

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:14.790
They came all this way to see you.

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:16.700
Right...

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:18.040
So, what do you want?

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:19.620
I don't want my body to get cold,

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:21.450
so I'd like to get this over with
as quickly as possible.

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:24.870
I told you! I want to know why
you suddenly transferred schools.

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:27.290
Just when we were ready
skate together as a team!

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:31.870
I want to know, too, as the leader of the club.

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:33.740
Why, Himekawa?

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:38.540
Because <i>that</i> guy came.

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:39.200
"That guy"?

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:39.870
This guy?

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:40.950
I knew it...

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:43.620
Because Maeshima was there, I left.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.080
Wait, me?!

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:48.040
Sorry! Did I do something weird?!

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:52.790
At that club match, I thought
I was able to do my best jump ever.

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:54.790
But that wasn't it.

00:08:54.790 --> 00:08:58.990
At the time, I was trying to be better than you,
who were skating as you pleased.

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:04.040
But as I tried to beat your speed,
agility, and expressiveness,

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:08.330
I was pulled along,
and the result was that jump.

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:11.290
What's wrong with that? It's normal, isn't it?

00:09:11.290 --> 00:09:12.950
It aggravated me!

00:09:12.950 --> 00:09:16.080
It felt like I was being controlled
by someone, and it gave me the creeps!

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:17.660
I realized then

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:20.240
that I was the one who had to control myself,

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:21.790
not someone like you!

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:24.950
That's why I came back
to skate with Coach Kumada.

00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:27.950
In order to reexamine myself.

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:30.450
Is this good enough for you?
I need to practice, so...

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:32.950
What the hell?! I don't get it!

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:34.540
What am I supposed to do?

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:35.970
What can I do so that you'll come bac--

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:37.370
No, it's not like that.

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:38.700
What?

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:41.580
But it looks like it's no use asking more.

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:45.830
Hey, do you think I'd give up
an important asset so easily?

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:47.080
That's not my problem.

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:50.580
Himekawa, I understand your situation.

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:53.040
Let's meet next at nationals.

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:55.620
Captain Terauchi, Mochizuki, sir,

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:59.240
thank you for everything
you've done for me up until now.

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:02.410
Sho, are you really going to leave it at that?

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:04.040
What?!

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:04.870
What is it?

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:06.540
It doesn't look like they'll
make it back tonight,

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:09.290
so the captain and the others
are staying at a hot springs inn.

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:10.870
What? No fair!

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:16.740
Will you stop sulking already?

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:19.290
My calculations got messed up, too, you know.

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:21.740
I have to think about new
positions and formations now.

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:23.330
That's not what it is.

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:25.160
Then, what is it?

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:28.910
That match was really fun for me.

00:10:28.910 --> 00:10:30.450
Jonouchi and Himekawa...

00:10:30.450 --> 00:10:32.950
Skating together with them,

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:36.410
with Himekawa taking the best part
for himself in that last jump...

00:10:38.410 --> 00:10:40.990
Someone else landed the last move,

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:43.910
but it still felt really good...

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:47.700
It made me think that things were
going to get even more fun, but...

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:50.870
Oh, good.

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:55.040
The last dinner service here was pretty late,
so I thought it'd work out somehow.

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:56.080
Thanks.

00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:58.040
I looked really hard, you know.

00:10:58.040 --> 00:11:00.540
To find a place that wouldn't use up
too much of our club budget, too.

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:03.870
We just have to buy souvenirs
for Akimitsu and the others.

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:05.950
Thanks for the food!

00:11:12.410 --> 00:11:15.080
Here, Shima. This is for you.

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:16.450
It's for the badge test.

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:18.620
You probably have one for singles,

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:21.160
but you don't have one
for skate-leading yet, do you?

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:26.040
You have to have one in order
to compete, so I applied for you.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:27.450
Make sure you go.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:29.660
Don't take it with chopsticks!

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:31.290
Oh, sorry! I just...

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:32.490
Sho, you know...

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:33.330
What is it?

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:37.620
You're very captain-like when
Vice-Captain Kiriyama isn't around.

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:38.210
Why is that?

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:40.160
Huh? Am I that different?

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:41.330
Yeah.

00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:42.910
I'm different, huh...?

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:52.980
A few days later
At the badge test venue

00:11:56.120 --> 00:11:58.120
Am I the only high schooler?

00:11:58.120 --> 00:12:01.240
Usually, you take your badge test
when you're a kid, right?

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:03.290
So most of the people taking
the test are in elementary school.

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:04.700
By the way, I have mine already.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:05.830
Traitor.

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:08.490
Anyway, why did <i>I</i> have to come with you?

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:09.740
Hurry up so I can go home.

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:11.290
Come on, he'll be done in no time.

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:15.120
I see. I mean, of course you'd pass
in one go, right, Maeshima?

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:18.540
You used to be a genius, and you must
feel refreshed after the hot springs.

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:20.790
Don't put weird pressure on me.

00:12:20.790 --> 00:12:23.240
--Hey, why are you here?
--Can I have your autograph?

00:12:23.240 --> 00:12:26.540
Okay, okay, wait your turn.

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:27.990
Huh? That's...

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:31.120
Okay, next.

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:33.200
Oh, you want it on your shirt? No problem.

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:34.120
Stop that.

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:35.790
Oh, you don't have to be embarrassed.

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:37.040
I said, I don't want one!

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:39.700
Huh? Oh, you're from Ionodai--

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:41.660
And who the hell are you?

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:44.370
You don't know who Noa is?

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:45.740
Dummy! Dummy!

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:46.370
What'd you say?!

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:46.990
Stop that.

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:48.240
They're on the same level.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:50.160
This is Noa Kuonji.

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:54.040
He used to live abroad and has won
a bunch of Canadian tournaments.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:56.410
After you quit figure skating,
he came back to Japan,

00:12:56.410 --> 00:13:00.240
and he's made a name for himself
as Shinozaki's rival.

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:01.330
Rival...

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:04.450
But he's never beat Shinozaki at a competition,
so he's been forever second.

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:10.290
Your nickname's "Number Two Prince," right?

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:12.330
Everyone knows, you know?

00:13:12.330 --> 00:13:16.540
That it's not always the oldest
brother who succeeds the throne.

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:18.620
You've accepted that you're
the Number Two Prince.

00:13:18.620 --> 00:13:21.040
And everyone wants to see it--

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:23.790
The younger brother who toils away
in obscurity until the end

00:13:23.790 --> 00:13:27.370
finally beating Shinozaki magnificently!

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:28.450
Yes.

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:31.160
But, he keeps appearing on variety shows on TV,

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:33.040
and whenever he does, he gets flamed online.

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:34.870
With people telling him to practice more.

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:39.540
That's all part of my strategy of how
I want to present myself to the world.

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:41.950
He reminds me of Jonouchi somehow.

00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:44.120
This guy's classier, though.

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:45.660
For the girls, number four:

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:48.330
In order to be popular,
you must train your core.

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:49.790
For the girls, number five:

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:52.290
In order to be popular,
you must style your hair.

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:56.080
I was originally planning on showing

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:59.490
a splendid come-from-behind victory
at my debut competition as a senior,

00:13:59.490 --> 00:14:02.990
but Shinozaki switched to skate-leading,

00:14:02.990 --> 00:14:04.540
so I had no choice but to come, too--

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:07.120
I understand what you are now.

00:14:07.120 --> 00:14:10.620
But <i>I'm</i> the one who will defeat Shinozaki!

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:11.700
Huh?

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:15.740
I'm sorry if I offended you.

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:19.120
But you're just starting as a high schooler,
and you want to beat Shinozaki?

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:20.700
I'm not just starting!

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:24.580
Huh? But you came to take your
skate-leading badge test, right?

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:27.740
For what it's worth, this guy's also
been skating since he was a kid.

00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:30.450
He took a break from figure
skating for a while, though.

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:33.740
In elementary school,
people called him Shinozaki's rival.

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:34.700
You?

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:36.290
Anyway, we're kind of the same, so--

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:37.910
Oh! Poor thing!

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:40.200
For your elementary school years
to be the peak of your life!

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:41.040
That's not it!

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:42.870
Hey, quiet down over there.

00:14:42.870 --> 00:14:44.990
If you're not going to register,
then you're being a nuisance, so go home.

00:14:44.990 --> 00:14:46.080
Oh, wait, I am!

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:47.990
I'm sorry! I'm going to register!

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:49.450
For the girls, number 23:

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:52.080
In order to be popular,
you must sweat wonderful sweat.

00:14:52.080 --> 00:14:56.160
And now, we will begin
the skate-leading badge test.

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:57.290
First, you will be tested in pairs.

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:59.660
Then, you will be tested individually.

00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:03.410
For the pair test, you will pair up
with the person next to you to skate.

00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:04.660
Rather than how together you are,

00:15:04.660 --> 00:15:06.910
we're looking to see if you
can match the other person...

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:08.830
You don't have to worry.

00:15:08.830 --> 00:15:11.740
I mean, I'll be with you.

00:15:11.740 --> 00:15:14.450
You two are the only
high schoolers taking the test.

00:15:14.450 --> 00:15:16.240
So of course you'd be paired up.

00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:17.740
Looking forward to it, Saejima.

00:15:17.740 --> 00:15:18.480
It's <i>Maeshima</i> !

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:20.580
Ahem!

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:22.870
Now, we'll start with the first pair.

00:15:22.870 --> 00:15:24.540
For the girls, number 147:

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:26.160
In order to be popular, you must win nationals.

00:15:26.160 --> 00:15:27.620
For the girls, number 148:

