00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:42.160
You know that 3-on-3 match
you had the other day?

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:44.870
I watched it. It was pretty good.

00:15:44.870 --> 00:15:46.290
Huh? Oh, really?

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:47.490
Thanks!

00:15:47.490 --> 00:15:48.420
He's so weak to flattery.

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:49.950
Shh.

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:54.200
I didn't switch to skate-leading
just because I felt like it.

00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:55.370
Oh, really?

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:57.490
It doesn't feel right if I don't win.

00:15:57.490 --> 00:16:00.660
That's why it's true that
I'm here chasing after Shinozaki.

00:16:00.660 --> 00:16:02.740
But that's just half of it.

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:05.740
What do you think the other half is?

00:16:05.740 --> 00:16:09.450
I want to use my celebrity to get
people excited about figure skating!

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:09.900
Huh?

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:12.290
Well, people do notice you.

00:16:12.290 --> 00:16:13.870
No matter the sport,

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:18.040
in order to revitalize the sport,
you need a story that's easy to understand.

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:22.950
The glorious star athletes,
rivals vying with each other.

00:16:22.950 --> 00:16:25.080
I will be the driving force in that story.

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:28.370
That's why I give interviews
and have people remember my name

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:32.700
and have them watch actual competitions
where they can be deeply moved.

00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:35.200
It's all for skating.

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:36.580
No matter how much I'm ridiculed for it,

00:16:36.580 --> 00:16:41.160
I will get as much publicity as I can
and fight against my rival, Shinozaki.

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:44.740
I have the resolve to do that.

00:16:44.740 --> 00:16:47.540
Will you join me? On the thorny path of glory?

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:48.370
Huh?

00:16:48.370 --> 00:16:50.370
Skate on the same team as me.

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:53.120
Since you were once called Shinozaki's rival,

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:55.870
even if you're not that good,
it'll create drama.

00:16:55.870 --> 00:16:56.990
What do you think?

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:59.290
"Not that good"?

00:16:59.290 --> 00:17:01.540
Next, pair number six.

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:03.290
Think about it.

00:17:05.160 --> 00:17:06.490
Shinozaki.

00:17:06.490 --> 00:17:08.120
Hey!

00:17:08.120 --> 00:17:08.950
Yes?

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:12.370
Apparently, that Kuonji's
going to do skate-leading.

00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:14.660
At a school in Kanagawa.

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:19.490
All your old rivals seem
to be gathering, one after another.

00:17:19.490 --> 00:17:21.540
How are you feeling?

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:23.200
Kuonji...

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:31.240
What the heck? We're not doing a spin here?

00:17:31.240 --> 00:17:33.450
It's my first time seeing Maeshima in pairs,

00:17:33.450 --> 00:17:35.370
but he's skating properly!

00:17:35.370 --> 00:17:36.700
Not really...

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:41.290
This guy's getting in the way when
I'm trying to expand to the outside.

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:43.370
What the heck? What the heck?

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:44.790
This isn't fun at all.

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:46.450
This isn't my timing.

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:50.040
It's all right. Come, leave everything to me.

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:52.540
It feels gross, damn it!

00:17:52.540 --> 00:17:56.370
I was the one who had to control myself!

00:17:56.370 --> 00:17:57.910
I get it now...

00:17:59.370 --> 00:18:00.870
Okay, that's enough.

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:09.700
Good work. You didn't make any mistakes.

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:12.290
You've cleared the first hurdle.

00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:13.290
You know--

00:18:13.290 --> 00:18:15.540
Keep it to yourself. This is a test.

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:17.290
I know that.

00:18:17.290 --> 00:18:19.040
Kuonji.

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:21.160
I won't be on your team.

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:23.160
Oh? Too bad.

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:26.410
Next, we'll start the individual lead test.

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.290
Let's start with examinee number one.

00:18:30.950 --> 00:18:33.660
For... the girls...

00:18:33.660 --> 00:18:37.450
Now, it's finally Kuonji's turn.

00:18:43.450 --> 00:18:46.790
Oh? Isn't this Himekawa's?

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:49.120
I need to send this to him, too.

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:50.490
Do you remember the order of the choreography?

00:18:50.490 --> 00:18:51.620
I remember.

00:18:51.620 --> 00:18:52.740
Do you need to make any changes?

00:18:52.740 --> 00:18:53.950
No.

00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:57.410
Listen, for a badge test,

00:18:57.410 --> 00:19:00.620
you just have to skate the compulsory
skills in the prescribed time.

00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:02.530
Even if you make a few mistakes,
it won't affect whether you pass or fail--

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:04.200
I know already.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:05.660
I've taken a badge test before.

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:07.700
When I let go of your reins, though...

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:08.910
What is it?

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:13.490
Wow, this seems super easy for him.

00:19:13.490 --> 00:19:15.410
It's like straight out of a textbook.

00:19:17.160 --> 00:19:18.740
Next is the last skill.

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:21.450
He did it!

00:19:21.450 --> 00:19:23.240
Noa, you're so cool!

00:19:23.240 --> 00:19:24.450
Perfect.

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:26.160
He has a lot of time left over, too,

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:28.700
so he can just do some easy skating
for the rest, and then he's done.

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:38.040
This isn't on the test...

00:19:38.040 --> 00:19:39.240
He's not done yet.

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:45.620
I will make skate-leading into
entertainment everyone can enjoy!

00:19:51.240 --> 00:19:53.200
Was that a quadruple flip just now?

00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:55.490
In addition to the test skills...
He did it so easily...

00:19:55.490 --> 00:19:57.700
That guy's picking a fight.

00:19:57.700 --> 00:20:00.910
He's saying he's as good as Shinozaki.

00:20:00.910 --> 00:20:02.540
Interesting...

00:20:02.540 --> 00:20:05.240
My frustration was building up, anyway!

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:06.830
W-Wait, sorry!

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:09.240
I accidentally egged you on like I usually do.

00:20:09.240 --> 00:20:10.990
Listen, this is a test.

00:20:10.990 --> 00:20:12.490
Make sure you do what you're supposed to do--

00:20:12.490 --> 00:20:13.830
Next! Number 13!

00:20:13.830 --> 00:20:15.160
Here!

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:16.540
Hey, wait--!

00:20:17.580 --> 00:20:19.330
You really did it this time.

00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:24.540
Do it. Do it like we planned.

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:27.660
Do it <i>exactly</i> as planned. Do it...!

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:33.330
That mongrel...

00:20:33.330 --> 00:20:36.160
Why is he doing moves
not in the compulsory skills?

00:20:36.160 --> 00:20:39.120
Not bad. Maeshima, huh?

00:20:41.870 --> 00:20:43.870
You failed your badge test?!

00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:46.290
You're an idiot. There's an idiot here.

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:47.660
I didn't fail.

00:20:47.660 --> 00:20:49.330
I just almost didn't pass...

00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:50.950
More precisely, you were last place.

00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:52.660
I can't believe you were able
to recover after that.

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:54.330
Worse than elementary schoolers!

00:20:54.330 --> 00:20:56.790
Oh, how the past genius has fallen!

00:20:56.790 --> 00:20:58.660
That's why I told you--

00:20:58.660 --> 00:21:01.790
You have to be conscious
of your other self watching you,

00:21:01.790 --> 00:21:02.950
so you can look at yourself objectively--

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:05.620
I don't know what you're
talking about, but I'm sorry, okay?

00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:06.910
What?!

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:07.410
What's wrong?

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:10.410
Oh, I just saw on the news

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:14.410
that Kuonji formed a new
skate-leading team with some idols!

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:15.790
What?!

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:19.450
Why did you decided to team up with Mi*Leon?

00:21:19.450 --> 00:21:21.950
Partly because we go to the same school,

00:21:21.950 --> 00:21:23.910
but also because, since they're idols,

00:21:23.910 --> 00:21:26.870
they have a great sense of rhythm
and excellent expressiveness.

00:21:26.870 --> 00:21:29.870
I'm the only one with figure skating experience,

00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:32.830
but we're seriously aiming to win nationals!

00:21:32.830 --> 00:21:34.450
Please watch us!

00:21:34.450 --> 00:21:36.330
Here we go!

00:21:36.330 --> 00:21:39.040
Why did we form a team?

00:21:39.040 --> 00:21:41.700
To give you our hearts.

00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:44.490
"Mi*Leon" "Noa Kuonji"

00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:47.120
--Mi*Leon!
--Noa!

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:44.490
"Mi*Leon aims for the Grand Prix with Noa Kuonji"

00:21:47.120 --> 00:21:50.740
We can't take our eyes off
of Team Mi*Leon, led by Kuonji.

00:21:50.740 --> 00:21:56.200
We plan to follow the five of them
and show you their progress,

00:21:56.200 --> 00:21:56.960
so look forward to it!

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:58.290
It's more of a variety show than news,

00:21:58.290 --> 00:21:59.950
but it must be what
he was talking about back then...

00:21:59.950 --> 00:22:01.330
Yeah.

00:22:01.330 --> 00:22:02.090
Oh?

00:22:02.090 --> 00:22:05.920
Noa Kuonji, Mi*Leon form skate-leading team

00:22:02.160 --> 00:22:06.040
Just you wait and see, Noa Kuonji.

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:50.950
Next Time

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:50.950
Bonds

00:23:38.240 --> 00:23:41.330
Coach, you did skate-leading
for a while, didn't you?

00:23:41.330 --> 00:23:42.200
You looked me up?

00:23:42.190 --> 00:23:43.190
And you were a wing.

00:23:43.190 --> 00:23:43.990
You looked me up?

00:23:43.990 --> 00:23:45.240
And you've had three
self-proclaimed girlfriends.

00:23:45.240 --> 00:23:46.120
You looked me up?!

00:23:46.120 --> 00:23:47.240
And self-proclaimed boyf--

00:23:47.240 --> 00:23:49.160
Ah, stop! Not the glasses!

00:23:49.160 --> 00:23:50.580
You looked up too much.
